From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kemp233 <kemp233@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 17:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] z96a: skip building rk3568-dahua-asi8212a.dtb

The rk3568-dahua-asi8212a.dts in kemp233/linux-rockchip@rk-6.1-rkr6.1
references labels (rgmii_phy0, rgmii_phy1, gmac1_miim, gmac1_tx_bus2,
gmac1_rx_bus2, gmac1_rgmii_clk, gmac1_hgmii_bus, vdd_logic) that no
longer exist in rk3568.dtsi / rk3568-pinctrl.dtsi after a refactor.
`make dtbs` fails with 8 phandle_references errors and aborts the
whole kernel build:

  ERROR (phandle_references): /rkvdec@fdf80200: Reference to
    non-existent node or label "vdd_logic"
  ERROR (phandle_references): /ethernet@fe010000: Reference to
    non-existent node or label "rgmii_phy1"
  ... (8 total)
  make[1]: *** [Makefile:1473: dtbs] Error 2

dahua is a security access control board (Dahua ASI8212A), unrelated
to z96a. Skip building its DTB by removing the Makefile entry. The
.dts source file remains in the tree but is not compiled.

z96a does not need this DTB (it uses its own
rockchip/rk3568-z96a-laptop-v2.dtb via the dts-directories config).
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
@@ -248,7 +248,6 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3568-rock-3a.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3568-swan1-w28.dtb
-dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3568-dahua-asi8212a.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3568-toybrick-sd0-android.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3568-toybrick-sd0-linux.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3568-toybrick-x0-android.dtb
